            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tori"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This sounded so awful I had to try it! I was very pleased to find it absolutely delicious. I will probably cut the amount in half next time (and just eat the remaining banana) as it was very rich. I also used nonfat dairy milk as I had no soy."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeani"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delicious! I used Lacinato (Dino) Kale - the dark green variety. I also added half an apple. The smoothie has more calories than I like to consume at once, but it was worth it for the packed nutrition. It served as a meal for me. I have a Blendtec so I packed ice in it as well - the texture was perfect - cold, thick, sweet and very tasty. Thank you Rice for this recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-10T09:29:09.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Andrea Torres MacScott"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Didn't expect it to be this tasty. \nI did blend the flaxseed by itself first so it is ground then I added all the other ingredients. I did not have soy milk handy so I just added plain water, and it works. Next time I will maybe skip the maple syrup as the banana very sweet!. recommended, my hubby liked it!",
            "datePublished": "2021-01-03T17:25:39.660Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeannine Dudzinski"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was my first kale smoothie. I did make some changes based on other reviews. I may not have used quite as much kale as called - used two handfuls of chopped kale, three ice cubes, some frozen blueberries, half of a banana, a tablespoon of local honey and filled the large ninja container with whole milk. Blended well - really yummy! Aside from the odd grayish color from the blueberries. I used the other half of the banana for a second batch to keep in the fridge for later.",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-13T12:13:26.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "im2blikgsus"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First I added the milk 6 oz vanilla soy milk with the organic kale and 3 ice cubes to blend on high. I stopped the blender after 90 seconds to add the frozen banana pieces. I processed on ice crush mode then stopped it again to added the flax seeds, natural maple syrup (tablespoon instead of a teaspoon). It was delicious! I'm making another one for breakfast tomorrow morning before I clean the blender.",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-16T11:13:42.643Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elizabeth Wohler Stowe"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was perfect! Not too sweet, not bitter.. I didn't have flax seed on hand so used 1 Tlb almond butter. I made it with the maple syrup the first time and it was very good. I switched out the syrup for 1/2 apple and I preferred the sweetness of the apple to the syrup. I also added a few ice cubes to make it icy cold. This will be my new staple for a green smoothie!",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-04T16:21:14.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LMS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe sounded so odd, I had to try it! Glad I did…it’s so tasty!...and I feel so proud of myself for getting in some veggies first thing in the morning. \n\nI tried the recipe as is, but my favorite is to use vanilla soy and skip the maple syrup. I also slice and freeze bananas ahead of time. Frozen bananas make the smoothie super creamy and cold. Sometimes I leave out the (ground) flax seed – it changes the color from fresh green to a sort of pond scum color which I don’t feel like facing some mornings. It also changes the texture, making it thicker. \n\nI agree with others…it’s a must to remove the stems from the kale; to blend well to get that smooth consistency, and to grind or use pre-ground flax seeds to get the benefit.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-16T19:34:50.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MWood"
            },
            "reviewBody": "2020: This smoothie was delicious, but the texture was chewy. I used a Ninja blender for several minutes and couldn't get a smoother texture. I made mine with unsweetened almond milk, ground flax seeds and added a handful of baby spinach. The smoothie tasted great, was quick to make and if it wasn't for the visible bits of kale, you wouldn't know it was in there. 2024: I tried this with my new Vitamix and the texture was smooth. It was a delicious afternoon snack that tastes so much better than it looks. Will definitely make often.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-19T22:12:06.325Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "livelove"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made it with 2 cups chopped kale (pre-chopped courtesy of Trader Joe's), 1 banana, and half a cup of Almond Milk - Vanilla (again thanks to TJs). SO DELISH! I put the kale in the freezer overnight, and banana in the fridge. tossed all of them together and was really really impressed by how delicious this is. I think this will be my staple breakfast smoothie. \nWill add the flax seeds, but no need for maple syrup for sure.",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-06T09:23:37.323Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good smoothie--made it great by using a frozen banana and adding 3 ice cubes. I left the flax out, just because I wasn't sure if my husband would like it, but I'm sure it would be good in this. I used unsweetened almond milk instead of soy and istead of maple syrup, I used a packet of Splenda. DH wants me to make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-10T19:48:56.673Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kiai"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Ground flax seeds are a thickening agent. I didn't have any but substituted hulled sunflower seeds. Used kefir instead of soy milk. Also don't care for sweet when there's fat so omitted syrup. Well, it's a different recipe, isn't it. Still good.",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-15T03:29:24.813Z"
          },
